Third-party components
======================

The components below are included in this repository, in the server container image, or in the Mac app. Each keeps its own license.

Silero VAD model
  File: crates/oah/models/silero_vad.onnx (compiled into the server and the Mac app)
  License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team
  License text: crates/oah/models/SILERO_LICENSE.txt
  Project: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad

ONNX Runtime, through the ort crate
  Used by the server and the Mac app for the voice activity detection model.
  ONNX Runtime: MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
  ort crate: MIT OR Apache-2.0.
  Project: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime and https://github.com/pykeio/ort

ffmpeg and ffprobe, Mac app
  Files: desktop-tauri/binaries/ffmpeg-<target> and ffprobe-<target>, built by desktop-tauri/scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh.
  The build is LGPL-only: it does not use --enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree or --enable-version3.
  ffmpeg 9.0.2: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. https://ffmpeg.org
  libopus 1.6.1 (linked into ffmpeg): BSD 3-Clause License. https://opus-codec.org
  LAME 4.0 (linked into ffmpeg as libmp3lame): GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.0. https://lame.sourceforge.io
  The corresponding source archives are fetched and checked by build-ffmpeg.sh. The release workflow attaches them to each GitHub Release.

ffmpeg and ffprobe, server container image
  The server image (deploy/Dockerfile) installs the Debian trixie ffmpeg package. Its license is the license of that Debian package, which can include GPL-licensed parts. The package copyright file is in the image at /usr/share/doc/ffmpeg/copyright.

Whisper model for browser transcription
  Not bundled. The browser downloads the onnx-community/whisper-base model from the Hugging Face hub the first time a user runs browser transcription. The model is a conversion of OpenAI's Whisper weights, released under the MIT License. The model files stay in the browser cache and are not part of this repository or the release.

Fonts
  No font files are bundled. The web app asks for the system font and the Geist font family by name and uses the operating system fallback when it is not installed.

Other dependencies
  The Rust crates in Cargo.lock and the npm packages in web/pnpm-lock.yaml and contract-tests/pnpm-lock.yaml are separate works. Each one carries its own license, which is stated in its package metadata.

